{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והארכת ימים", :translit "v'ha'archa yamim", :gloss "and you shall lengthen days"} {:he "בעולם שכולו ארוך", :translit "b'olam shekulo aruch", :gloss "in a world that is entirely long"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "והארכת ימים", :b "בעולם שכולו ארוך"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'a world that is entirely long' alludes to the world to come (olam ha-ba), whose reward is eternal, as distinguished from this world which is finite. Isaiah 64:3 speaks of what no eye has seen besides God, which the Sages interpret as referring to the world to come.", :sources ["Isaiah 64:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והארכת ימים", :translit "v'ha'archa yamim", :gloss "and you shall lengthen days"} {:he "כי תבנה בית חדש", :translit "ki tivne bayit chadash", :gloss "when you build a new house"} {:he "למען ייטב לך", :translit "l'ma'an yitav lach", :gloss "so that it may be good for you"} {:he "כי יפל הנופל ממנו", :translit "ki yipol ha-nofel mimenu", :gloss "when the fallen one falls from it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut (juxtaposition): והארכת ימים placed adjacent to כי תבנה בית חדש to connect length of days with building a parapet; and למען ייטב לך juxtaposed to כי יפל הנופל ממנו"}], :frame {:text "The command to send the mother bird promises length of days (Deuteronomy 22:7), yet the very next verse (Deuteronomy 22:8) discusses one who falls from a roof, which the Sages read as addressing a case where a person climbed a tree to fulfill the commandment of sending the mother bird and fell to his death. This raises the theological question of reward in this world, which the Talmud takes up directly: it teaches that the reward 'so that it may be good and your days will be long' refers to the world to come rather than this world.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 22:7" "Deuteronomy 22:8" "Deuteronomy 5:16"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "והארכת ימים", :a-value 732, :b "בעולם שכולו ארוך", :b-value 737, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Semikhut (juxtaposition): והארכת ימים placed adjacent to כי תבנה בית חדש to connect length of days with building a parapet; and למען ייטב לך juxtaposed to כי יפל הנופל ממנו", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:18.681369814Z", :model "glm-5.2"}